## Environment, Compute & Disk

- **Where you are**: an LSF batch job on the `{{ SITE }}` cluster. `nproc` reports how many cores
  it was given. There is no GPU and you do not need one.
- **Your own budget**: use at most **{{ CORES }} CPU cores** at any one time, whatever `nproc` says. The rest
  belong to the session hosting you — saturating the node will stall your own tool calls.
- **Per-candidate limit**: any single candidate program you run **must return within {{ BUDGET_S }} seconds**
  and may use **at most {{ P.cpus_per_candidate }} CPU core{{ 's' if P.cpus_per_candidate != 1 else '' }}**. Anything still running at **{{ KILL_S }} s** is killed and scores
  nothing. Pin your children (`taskset -c`, or `OMP_NUM_THREADS={{ P.cpus_per_candidate }} MKL_NUM_THREADS={{ P.cpus_per_candidate }}
  OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS={{ P.cpus_per_candidate }} NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS={{ P.cpus_per_candidate }}`) — an unpinned numpy/scipy build will happily grab
  every core on the node and make your own timings meaningless.
- With {{ CORES }} cores and {{ P.cpus_per_candidate }} core{{ 's' if P.cpus_per_candidate != 1 else '' }} per candidate you can hold **{{ PARALLEL }} candidates in flight at once**. Use that.
- **Python**: `{{ PYTHON }}` — Python 3.12 with numpy 2.5.1,
  scipy 1.18.0 and cvxpy 1.9.2 (solvers: CLARABEL, SCS, ECOS, ECOS_BB, SCIPY, HIGHS, OSQP).
  Use that interpreter, not a bare `python`. **Do not create another virtual environment** and do
  not try to install packages: this job has no outbound network, so every install attempt is a
  wasted turn. If you genuinely need a library that is not there, say so in your final report
  instead of working around it.
- **Disk**: write everything you produce into a folder called `run/` inside your working
  directory, and create it on your first write. The files already here (`INITIAL_PROMPT.md`,
  `eval.py`, `_official_evaluator.py`, `_adrs_track.json`, the input `.npy`) stay at the top level —
  read them there, do not move, copy or edit them. Keep the total under ~2 GB.

